    "note": "the fills are copper in parallel with the escapes, but a fill is not in the board file -- only its outline is -- so the escape is the only part that can be rated from the geometry that is.  Each secondary half leaves its pour at x 43 and reaches the drain land at x 46.87 through one 0.8 mm track and two 0.3 mm-drill vias in series, and escape_rating quotes that path in both bases (adiabatic I2t for a fault pulse, IPC-2221 chart for a continuous current) rather than blending them.  The via barrel binds the pulse number at either copper weight.  VSS is routed at signal width on purpose: it is the controller's source reference through the R1 Kelvin tap, not a current path."
