  "remaining_work": [
    "check the digitised land against a vendor CAD model or an IPC-7351 calculation when one is available: it is measured from Fig. 2 of the datasheet (max residual 4.9 um) but is still a redrawing, and neither this repository nor the sheet's board-pads figure says whether the lands are to IPC density level A, B or C",
    "widen the secondary escape before claiming more than a fault pulse: the 0.8 mm track and the two 0.3 mm-drill vias between the pour edge at x 43 and the drain land at x 46.87 are quoted in power_path.escape_rating, and at 1 oz the chart puts one half at about 2 A continuous.  IPC-2221 has no via-barrel term, so a continuous rating needs a barrel calculation from the fabricator's plating spec, not a wider chart lookup",
    "keep the VSS Kelvin tap (R1) off the power return -- the PGND pour is what must not creep up to it, and that is a fill question, not a track question",
    "confirm the copper weight with the fabricator: the package asks for 1 oz, which is what the escape_rating chart numbers are quoted at; 2 oz would raise the track figure but not the via barrel that binds the pulse number",
    "the fab package in pcb/sr_fault_validation/fab/ is exported and is still not an approval: the manifest binds the nine gerbers, the drill file and the DNP-excluded position CSV to the board hash and repeats the escape rating as a stated limit, and the export fails if a layer it asked for is missing or a DNP part is still in the CSV.  hardware_built and fabrication_approved stay false until a person signs, and the 1 oz in it is a request to the fabricator, not a measurement"
  ]
